course: dictionary
lesson: 13233
title: Describing texture
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something feels or looks when you touch it. Gelatinous is one of them. It describes things that are thick, soft and wobbly, like jelly. «The frogspawn in the pond was a gelatinous mass.» You can picture it: a soft clump that wobbles when you touch it.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The jellyfish drifted past, soft and gelatinous.» Soft and drifting are clues, and they point to something wobbly like jelly. Swap in your meaning: "soft and jelly-like" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Gelatinous can also describe what something is made of. Gelatine is the clear substance that makes jelly set. «The cold stock had turned gelatinous in the pot.» The stock has set and now wobbles like jelly. Monsters in stories are often gelatinous too, which makes them sound slimy.
fact: Gelatinous means thick, soft and wobbly, like jelly.
fact: It can also mean made of or containing gelatine, the clear substance that sets jelly.
fact: In science, gelatinous describes frogspawn, jellyfish, some fungi, slime and the layer around chia seeds.
fact: Phrases you may meet: gelatinous mass, gelatinous texture.
fact: Gelatinous is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «a gelatinous blob».
exercise: «The frogspawn in the pond was a gelatinous mass.» What does gelatinous mean? | Hard and shiny like metal | Dry and crumbly like sand | *Thick, soft and wobbly like jelly
exercise: «The slime monster oozed across the floor, gelatinous and grey.» Which word is a clue that gelatinous means wobbly and slimy? | floor | grey | monster | *oozed
exercise: Which of these is gelatinous? | A dry biscuit | *A bowl of set jelly | A wooden spoon | A cup of cold water
test: «The chia seed was coated in a gelatinous layer when it touched the water.» What does gelatinous mean here? | Sharp and pointy | *Soft and slippery like jelly | Very loud
test: Ella says gelatinous is just another word for jelly. Why is that not quite right? | They mean exactly the same, so there is no difference at all | *Gelatinous is an adjective that describes something as like jelly, while jelly is the food itself | Jelly is an adjective and gelatinous is a food
exam: «The gelatinous blob in the story wobbled towards the children.» What does gelatinous tell you about the blob? | Tiny and invisible | *Wobbly and soft, like jelly | Made of metal and very hard | Loud and angry
